<title>SINGAPORE: Transmarco sells part of telecom stake.</title>
<headline>Transmarco sells part of telecom stake.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transmarco Ltd said on Friday it has sold part of its stake in a Sri Lanka telecommunications project for about Singapore $15.1 million.</p>
<p>Transmarco said it has reduced its 72.95 percent in Lanka Bell, a company which has a licence to operate a telecom system in Sri Lanka, to 33.69 percent after the sale.</p>
<p>The sale of the Lanka Bell stake was to Korean Telecom.</p>
<p>Transmarco said the sale of the stake is at a premium of about S$3 million to the cost of its original investment in Lanka Bell of about S$12.1 million.</p>
<p>- Singapore Newsroom 65-8703080</p>
